course: dictionary
lesson: 8608
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word scrap is a good example. In «Worms, fungi and bacteria break kitchen scraps down into rich compost», scraps are bits of food left over, because kitchen waste is what breaks down.
explain: Read the words around the word and ask what would fit. In «The council will scrap the old cars», the sentence is about getting rid of things, so scrap means to get rid of or recycle. Try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Scrap can also be a small fight, but this is informal, so it is used in chatty speech and stories. «Unlike a playground scrap, many ordinary people lose their homes» shows that a playground scrap is a small fight, which is far less serious than a war.
fact: Scrap can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action).
fact: A scrap is a small piece of something, such as «a scrap of paper» or cloth.
fact: Scraps are bits of food left over after a meal.
fact: Scrap metal is old metal that is thrown away or recycled.
fact: To scrap something means to get rid of it or cancel it. Informally, a scrap is a small fight or argument.
exercise: «Worms, fungi and bacteria break kitchen scraps down into rich compost.» What are kitchen scraps? | Pieces of cloth for sewing | A small fight in the kitchen | *Bits of food left over after a meal | Old metal thrown away
exercise: «Unlike a playground scrap, many ordinary people lose their homes.» What is a playground scrap? | Old metal for recycling | *A small fight | A new playground | Bits of food from lunch
exercise: «The trip was scrapped.» What does scrapped mean? | *Cancelled | Made longer | Painted a bright colour | Finished with a big party
test: «Gulls really do squabble for every scrap, even snatching chips from a person's hand.» What is a scrap here? | A fight between two gulls | A large seagull | *A small bit of food | A piece of metal from a shed
test: «The council will scrap the old cars.» What does scrap mean? | *Get rid of them, so they can be recycled | Paint them bright colours | Wash them carefully | Sell them to a museum
exam: Which sentence uses scrap to mean cancel? | *They decided to scrap the picnic because of the rain | Ella put the kitchen scraps in the bin | They found a scrap of cloth for the collage | Dad took the old bike to the scrap yard
